# Project management

Managers set up projects, populate the annotation queue, and control who has
access.

## Landing page

When you log in as a manager without an annotator or curator assignment, you are
taken directly to the **Project Management** page for your project. If you also
have an annotator or curator role, you will first see a hub where you can choose
which activity to start.

## Adding articles

Go to **Documents** in the sidebar. Enter one or more PubMed IDs or DOIs and click
**Add**. If an article is available on PubMed Central it is fetched automatically
and added to the project queue.

## Managing ontologies

Under **Ontologies** you can import OWL files that define the entity types and
relations allowed in the project. Imported ontologies determine which classes
annotators can choose from.

## Managing users

Open **Users** in the sidebar.

### Adding an existing user

Type any part of the user's email address into the search field. After a short
pause, a dropdown appears with all matching accounts. Click the account you want
to add, then select a role (**Annotator** or **Curator**) and click
**Add to project**.

### Creating a new account

If the person does not yet have an account, click **Create new account for …** at
the bottom of the search dropdown. A form appears with:

- **Email** — pre-filled from your search, but fully editable. Change it to the
  user's actual address if needed.
- **Role** — choose Annotator or Curator.
- **Initial passphrase** — a suggested passphrase is generated automatically.
  Copy it with the clipboard button and share it with the new user; they will use
  it to log in for the first time. Click the refresh button to generate a
  different passphrase if you prefer.

Click **Create & add** to create the account and add it to the project in one
step. The passphrase is shown once after creation — make sure to share it before
navigating away.

### Removing a role

In the member list, click **Remove Annotator** or **Remove Curator** next to a
user to take away that role. The user's account itself is not affected.
